%description:

TcpSessionApp.tClose = -1: the application closes the connection at once after its last send.

The claim (TcpSessionApp.ned): the application issues a TCP CLOSE at tClose, but not before
its last SEND; with a time before the last SEND, -1 for example, the CLOSE follows the last
SEND at once. The code: TcpSessionApp::sendData() schedules the CLOSE at max(tClose, now)
after the last command. Before this test, the NED said that -1 issues no CLOSE (finding PF-1
of doc/project/evidence/model/tcp/parameters.md).

Host under test: host1, with TcpSessionApp, which opens a connection to host2:1000 at 0.1 s
and sends 10000 bytes at 0.2 s, with tClose = -1; host2 reads the data with TcpEchoApp and
sends nothing back. Observation: level 1, host1 sends a FIN before 1 s, and host2
acknowledges it after the 10000 bytes (ISS + 10002), so the FIN follows the last byte of the
data. With tClose = 1000s, no FIN comes in the run.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSessionAppCloseAfterLastSend")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.finBit == true")
             .describe("the FIN of host1, after its last send at 0.2 s")
             .within(0.9))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 10002")
             .describe("the ACK of host2 for the FIN after the 10000 bytes")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSessionAppCloseAfterLastSend compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
network = inet.protocoltest.TapPairNetwork
sim-time-limit = 10s
seed-set = 0
**.tcp.typename = "Tcp"
*.host1.numApps = 1
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpSessionApp"
*.host1.app[0].connectAddress = "host2"
*.host1.app[0].connectPort = 1000
*.host1.app[0].tOpen = 0.1s
*.host1.app[0].tSend = 0.2s
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 10000B
*.host1.app[0].tClose = -1s    # the value under test
*.host2.numApps = 1
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpEchoApp"
*.host2.app[0].localPort = 1000
*.host2.app[0].echoFactor = 0

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSessionAppCloseAfterLastSend: PASS
